# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build artifacts
bin/
ui/dist/

# rumdl cache (rumdl also self-ignores this via a nested .gitignore)
.rumdl_cache/

# Throwaway Phase-0 contract spike (never committed)
spike/

# Playwright artifacts (failure traces/screenshots can capture rendered plan
# text — they stay local, never committed)
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/
.last-run.json

# Logs / OS cruft
*.log
.DS_Store

# Nested worktrees (parity with the repo root)
.claude/worktrees/

# Project CLAUDE.md files are intentionally NOT contributed. In practice they
# tend to be overly broad and not helpful to everyone else. Before adding one,
# ask yourself two things:
#   1. Should this be a rule instead? Scoped, discoverable guidance belongs in
#      .claude/rules/ — see https://code.claude.com/docs/en/memory (the
#      "Organize rules with .claude/rules/" section).
#   2. Is it a net benefit to everyone working on the project, or just your own
#      preference? Personal preferences belong in your global ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md
#      or in .claude/settings.local.json, not in the repo.
/CLAUDE.md
